2. **Frequency and Duty Cycle Calculation**:
   - With $SYSCLK = PCLK2 = 170\text{ MHz}$ and APB2 prescaler = 1, the timer input clock is $f_{\text{TIM1CLK}} = 170\text{ MHz}$.
   - To achieve $f_{\text{PWM}} = 20\text{ kHz}$:
     $$\text{ARR} + 1 = \frac{f_{\text{TIM1CLK}}}{(\text{PSC} + 1) \cdot f_{\text{PWM}}} = \frac{170\,000\,000}{(0 + 1) \cdot 20\,000} = 8500 \implies \text{ARR} = 8499$$
   - For a 25% duty cycle in PWM mode 1 (output active when $\text{CNT} < \text{CCR1}$):
     $$\text{CCR1} = 0.25 \cdot (\text{ARR} + 1) = 0.25 \cdot 8500 = 2125$$
